sw/scripts/ - CLI-driven pipelines
==================================

    cgra-bench.sh   stress-benchmark the whole .cgra standard library on a
                    device and print a structured report (a throughput +
                    link-stats table per vector size) plus a JSON artifact.
                    Drives the cgra CLI (`benchall`), so it needs no FPGA to
                    dry-run.

Use it
------
    make bench                       # DEV=sim, sweeps 256/1024/4096
    make bench DEV=auto              # after `cgra probe` on a real board
    make bench SIZES="1024 8192" REPEAT=100 DEV=/dev/ttyUSB1

    # or directly:
    DEV=sim sw/scripts/cgra-bench.sh

Knobs (env or `make bench VAR=...`): DEV, SIZES, REPEAT, CGRA, STDLIB, OUT.
With DEV=auto it discovers + correctness-checks the FPGA (`cgra probe`) before
benchmarking, so only a trusted device is measured. Output artifact defaults to
../build/benchmark.json.

The whole-program C profiling of the CLI (gprof/perf/callgrind) lives in the
sw.mk targets, not here: `make gprof | perf | callgrind`.
